/ "Change" (TransactionsController#categories) on the list and the transaction page: a link that loads one category
/ picker per line into the empty Turbo Frame after it, only when asked for (never a lazy frame per row, which would
/ fire one request per visible row). A transaction booked from a receipt links to the receipt instead (its lines are
/ rebuilt from the items on "Accept again"); a transfer leg has no lines and no control.
/ `link_params`: the list's filter ({ filter: {...} }) or { return_to: "page" }; `autofocus`: the focus comes back here.
- unless transaction.transfer_leg?
  - if transaction.receipt
    = ui_link_button "Change on the receipt", receipt_path(transaction.receipt), variant: :link, size: :sm, data: { turbo_prefetch: false }
  - else
    = ui_link_button categories_transaction_path(transaction, link_params), variant: :link, size: :sm, id: dom_id(transaction, :change_categories),
      "aria-label": "Change the categories of #{transaction_label(transaction)}", "aria-controls": dom_id(transaction, :categories),
      data: { turbo_frame: dom_id(transaction, :categories), turbo_prefetch: false, controller: ("autofocus" if local_assigns[:autofocus]) } do
      = ui_icon "pencil"
      span Change
    = turbo_frame_tag dom_id(transaction, :categories)
